==English==

===Etymology===
{{sense|unit of measure}} From {{bor|en|es|cuarto||[[quarter]]-[[sack]]}}, from {{der|en|la|quartus||[[fourth]], [[quarter]]}}. {{doublet|en|quart|quarter|cuarta}}, etc.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|historical}} A [[traditional]] [[Spanish]] [[unit of measure|unit]] of [[dry measure]], [[equivalent]] to about 27.8 [[liter|L]].
# {{lb|en|historical}} A former Spanish coin (until 1866), worth one eighth of a [[real]].

